# Build context for the Dockerfiles. Dockerfile.native copies the whole tree (COPY . .) and the
# JVM ones copy jars out of */target, so target/ stays in. What is excluded here is local output
# that runs to tens of GB: benchmark runs and test gateways leave pre-allocated 200 MB journal
# segments behind, and without this every image build shipped them all to the Docker daemon.
benchmark/results/
**/journals/
**/*.r7f
**/*.flux
**/*.corrupt
**/node_modules/
.claude/
.idea/
